#import "../prelude.typ": *

#set heading(numbering: none)

= Syllabus and Overview

#fade[Michaelmas Term, 2026] #h(1fr) #fade[[24 Lectures]]

#h(1fr) #fade[[3 Lectures]]

Definition of a vector space (over $RR$ or $CC$), subspaces, the space spanned by a subset. Linear independence, bases, dimension. Direct sums and complementary subspaces. Quotient spaces.

#h(1fr) #fade[[4 Lectures]]

Linear maps, isomorphisms. Relation between rank and nullity. The space of linear maps from $U$ to $V$, representation by matrices. Change of basis. Row rank and column rank.

#h(1fr) #fade[[3 Lectures]]

Determinant and trace of a square matrix. Determinant of a product of two matrices and of the inverse matrix. Determinant of an endomorphism. The adjugate matrix.

#h(1fr) #fade[[4 Lectures]]

Eigenvalues and eigenvectors. Diagonal and triangular forms. Characteristic and minimal polynomials. Cayley–Hamilton Theorem over $CC$. Algebraic and geometric multiplicity of eigenvalues. Statement and illustration of Jordan normal form.

#h(1fr) #fade[[2 Lectures]]

Dual of a finite-dimensional vector space, dual bases and maps. Matrix representation, rank and determinant of dual map.

#h(1fr) #fade[[4 Lectures]]

Bilinear forms. Matrix representation, change of basis. Symmetric forms and their link with quadratic forms. Diagonalisation of quadratic forms. Law of inertia, classification by rank and signature. Complex Hermitian forms.

#h(1fr) #fade[[4 Lectures]]

Inner product spaces, orthonormal sets, orthogonal projection, $V = W plus.o W^perp$. Gram–Schmidt orthogonalisation. Adjoints. Diagonalisation of Hermitian matrices. Orthogonality of eigenvectors and properties of eigenvalues.
